Fillets: an OnSame end whose opposite contact ends on the prolonged edge
itself, short of the corner's vertex, cuts that edge there instead of
adding a prolongation along it; the prolonged edge is the face at the
end's edge with the opposite face, and a seam of the face at the end that
starts at the vertex runs on to the cut (mitcad#1359).

A plate's top edge rounded up to a boss whose cylinder the plate's flat
side goes on into tangentially, along their common vertical edge below the
corner's vertex: the rounding's contact on the top meets the boss's foot
short of the vertex (an OnSame end, the cylinder the face at the end, the
side the opposite face), and the contact on the side, at the plate's
height less the radius, touches the cylinder on that vertical edge (at 12
for a radius of 3). PerformOneCorner took that point for the end of the
edge's prolongation past the vertex and added the curve from the vertex
down to it (VARIANT1), the edge's own piece there again, and the edge was
not cut: the side's and the cylinder's wires ran along it twice, an
invalid result (self-intersecting wires, or an unorientable face). Now, where
the opposite contact's end lies on the prolonged edge (within 10 tolapp3d)
inside it and away from the vertex, no curve is added and the edge is cut
there, its part from the vertex lying under the blend, as an arc the
opposite contact ends on is cut (cutArcop).

Where the face at the end has a seam that ends at the vertex on the
prolonged edge's line (the cylinder's seam running up from the vertex, the
edge left from it), the face goes on across that line from the vertex to
the cut: the seam runs on along its line from the vertex to the cut, on
both of its sides, as patch 0931 runs it on to a cap's crossing (a curve on
the face's iso-line through the seam, here run the way the seam's curve
runs and used on each side as the seam is there, which is how the faces'
builder chains the pieces of a seam), and the seam itself is kept from the
vertex on, where every other edge is cut away.

The prolonged edge was the first edge of the face at the end at the vertex
other than the arc the blend's contact ends on; at the vertex where the
cylinder's seam starts that was the seam, and the end was built along it.
The edge the face at the end shares with the opposite face is taken first
(at a vertex of three edges it is the only other one).

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_boss_tangent.cpp, the plate's top edge
rounded with 1, 3 and 6 with the cylinder's seam at either vertex and on
the body MitCad's sketch and extrusions build (MITCAD_GEOMETRY_CASES):
valid, the material removed as the exact one within 1e-6 of it.

Upstream: new.

